---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import raw from '../../../data/players/daniel-hammond.json';
import { playerStatsSchema } from '../../lib/player-stats';
const data = playerStatsSchema.parse(raw);
---

<Layout title="Knights players" description="St. Louis Knights player profiles and game-by-game statistics.">
  <div class="page-heading">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">2013 ST. LOUIS KNIGHTS</span>
      <h1>Player profiles.</h1>
      <p>Individual game stats and season progress.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="season-chip">2026–27</span>
  </div>
  <article class="panel player-card">
    <span class="number" aria-label="Number 11">
      11
    </span>
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">DEFENSE · SHOOTS LEFT</span>
      <h2>
        <a href="/players/daniel-hammond/">Daniel Hammond</a>
      </h2>
      <p>{data.games.length} imported games · Hudl Instat</p>
      <a href="/players/daniel-hammond/">View profile & game stats →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
  <p class="coverage">
    Hudl has plenty of useful information, but digging through it—especially on a phone—can be a challenge.
    Daniel’s profile is a first experiment in making those stats easier to explore and more interesting to
    follow throughout the season. Interested in having your player’s profile here? Let Chris know, and he’ll
    provide instructions for downloading and sending your player’s stats.
  </p>
</Layout>
<style>
  .player-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 28px;
    max-width: 650px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .number {
    font-size: 64px;
    font-weight: 850;
    color: var(--red);
    letter-spacing: -4px;
  }
  .player-card p {
    margin: 10px 0;
  }
  .coverage {
    margin-top: 24px;
    max-width: 650px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .player-card {
      padding: 20px;
      gap: 18px;
    }
    .number {
      font-size: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>
